\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {11}{\ignorespaces \textbf  {Left:} looks that pass the stage-1 cut, in the plane of the two half-dataset significances. Real signals and coherent mismodellings populate the same locus; per-run artefacts sit on the $Z_B \approx 0$ axis and die at the claim bar. \textbf  {Right:} the resulting spurious-claim rate. The two defects are \emph  {identical} to a single-stage scan --- one curve, by construction --- and the split separates them by changing the scaling from $\epsilon $ to $\epsilon ^{2}$ for the incoherent one alone.\relax }}{23}{figure.caption.35}\protected@file@percent }
